  "query_preview": "../Wednesday through Saturday/... A broad upper-level \ntrough continues to make its way across the panhandle Wednesday \nand Thursday, which is likely to drive an active, wetter pattern \nthrough the middle of the week. Low level troughing, that looks \nto build off of western Alaska, and the moisture associated with \nit push eastward across the gulf early Wednesday morning which is \nexpected to bring wide spread rain to the panhandle on Wednesday \nafternoon. Rain is likely to last through most of the day on \nThursday before the main frontal boundary shifts east. There is a \nchance for an area of high pressure to build sometime early in the\nday Friday which could bring a brief period of clearing, \nespecially over the northern panhandle. Confidence in rain \nchances then increases later in the day on Friday as another front\napproaches the panhandle from across the the gulf. Rain is \nexpected to persist through the rest of the period. Rain \naccumulations through the period are expected to be light to \nmoderate, with coastal locations likely to receive higher \nrainfall totals. Temperatures are likely to be in the upper 50s to\n60s with low diurnal ranges due to constant cloud cover.",
